<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-010> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) regeneration as a lawful growth process — Durbin/Ellis tadpole tail curves (Rana (Lithobates) clamitans tadpoles (Ellis 1909); Rana tadpoles (Durbin 1909))",
        "Thompson (1917) regeneration as a lawful growth process — Durbin/Ellis tadpole tail curves faithfully reproduces Rana (Lithobates) clamitans tadpoles (Ellis 1909); Rana tadpoles (Durbin 1909) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-010-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-010-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-010-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-010-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-010-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-010-6> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) thompson/claims/t1917-010_the-rate-of-growth.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Rana (Lithobates) clamitans tadpoles (Ellis 1909); Rana tadpoles (Durbin 1909) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-010_the-rate-of-growth.py> ;
    schema:about "Rana (Lithobates) clamitans tadpoles (Ellis 1909); Rana tadpoles (Durbin 1909)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A mechanistic model of tail regeneration, or that the exponential/Gompertz laws are the true generative process rather than descriptive fits to 7-10 points per series",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Least-squares fits of exponential-approach, hyperbolic (L_inf - c/t), logistic and Gompertz laws to the printed tables; OLS decay exponents on Thompson's interpolated increments; Ellis absolute-regenerate scaling and linearly interpolated isochrones with log-log slopes",
        "reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) p. 148 reproduces Ellis's series O/P/R/S (12-57 % of tail removed) and constructs Fig. 40 isochrones that 'approximate in form to a cubic parabola' and diverge at 75 % removed",
        "reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) pp. 139-145 reproduces Durbin's Exp. II and Exp. IV regenerated-length tables and asserts V falls 'inversely as the square of the time' with log V approximately linear (Fig. 37) and an inflection 'about the seventh day' in Exp. IV",
        "transfer_boundary: No transfer to a modern dataset: the pre-scouted Dryad lizard dataset is a DATASET_MISMATCH and is excluded from the verdict" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-010_the-rate-of-growth.py; output: docs/media/t1917_010_the_rate_of_growth_comparison.png; organism: Rana (Lithobates) clamitans tadpoles (Ellis 1909); Rana tadpoles (Durbin 1909); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) pp. 139-145 reproduces Durbin's Exp. II and Exp. IV regenerated-length tables and asserts V falls 'inversely as the square of the time' with log V approximately linear (Fig. 37) and an inflection 'about the seventh day' in Exp. IV | Thompson (1917) p. 148 reproduces Ellis's series O/P/R/S (12-57 % of tail removed) and constructs Fig. 40 isochrones that 'approximate in form to a cubic parabola' and diverge at 75 % removed; reconstructed_in_script: Least-squares fits of exponential-approach, hyperbolic (L_inf - c/t), logistic and Gompertz laws to the printed tables; OLS decay exponents on Thompson's interpolated increments; Ellis absolute-regenerate scaling and linearly interpolated isochrones with log-log slopes; transfer_boundary: No transfer to a modern dataset: the pre-scouted Dryad lizard dataset is a DATASET_MISMATCH and is excluded from the verdict; does_not_claim: A mechanistic model of tail regeneration, or that the exponential/Gompertz laws are the true generative process rather than descriptive fits to 7-10 points per series]; other sources: On Growth and Form <https://archive.org/details/ongrowthform1917thom>; phenomenon_size: 64 µm (6.42e-05 m, log10=-4.192 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 64 µm to 9.7 cm): 64 µm:rana-temporaria-bioelectric-polarity, 227 µm:rana-temporaria-vertex-packing, 2.2 mm:rana-temporaria-turing-wavelength, 7.7 mm:rana-temporaria-clock-wavefront, 1.4 cm:rana-temporaria-morphogen-condensation, 1.7 cm:rana-temporaria-flux-canalization, 1.9 cm:rana-temporaria-elastic-buckling, 2.3 cm:rana-temporaria-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/jez.1400070302>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1002/jez.1400070303>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsbl.2019.0151> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-010-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-010-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-010-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-010-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-010-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-010-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-010-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-010-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-010-the-rate-of-growth-audit-thompson1917-t1917-010-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-010-the-rate-of-growth-audit-thompson1917-t1917-010-10>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-010-the-rate-of-growth-audit-thompson1917-t1917-010-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-010-the-rate-of-growth-audit-thompson1917-t1917-010-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-010-the-rate-of-growth-audit-thompson1917-t1917-010-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-010-the-rate-of-growth-audit-thompson1917-t1917-010-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-010-the-rate-of-growth-audit-thompson1917-t1917-010-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-010-the-rate-of-growth-audit-thompson1917-t1917-010-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-010-the-rate-of-growth-audit-thompson1917-t1917-010-8>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-28-t1917-010-the-rate-of-growth-audit-thompson1917-t1917-010-9> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "quantitative-empirical regenerative growth curves (Thompson 1917 Ch. III; Durbin 1909; Ellis 1909)" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 5.5e-01 .

